## Command evidence and applicability

{{COMMAND_PROVENANCE}}

Associate each exact command with triggering paths/behavior, repository/CI source,
prerequisites, side effects, and expected outputs. Unknown commands or applicability
are documentation gaps, not guesses. The matrix references commands above and
states when consumer/integration checks are required; do not duplicate commands.

{{VALIDATION_MATRIX}}

Start with focused checks; include required target and consumer/contract checks
when behavior crosses their boundaries. Report missing coverage. Prefer temporary
output/cache paths where supported; do not alter code merely to force a pass
outside the authorized scope.

If `.agents/ai/verification-routes.json` and its selector are installed, use them
to select candidate checks. Otherwise select directly from the commands above.
A selector does not authorize execution. Structured provenance and fingerprint
audits are optional maintenance tools, not prerequisites for routine checks.

## Diff checks and results

Run `git diff --check`; review relevant diff/status against the starting state.
Check for unintended, generated, private, or unrelated changes. Report each
executed check as pass/fail and required unexecuted checks as not-run, with the
reason and remaining risk. Required failures prevent a completion claim.

